 ## Background
-A-NeRF builds on NeRF [42] and uses appearance code design from [36, 49]. It was proposed to learn a generative neural body model from unlabelled monocular videos by extending Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs) with a skeleton to apply to time-varying and articulated motion [S2, unofficial]. The method addresses the ill-posed inverse problem of mapping 3D world coordinates to a canonical space for articulated bodies by overparameterizing with one embedding per bone [S2, unofficial].
+A-NeRF builds on NeRF [42] and uses appearance code design from [36, 49] [S2, unofficial]. It was proposed to learn a generative neural body model from unlabelled monocular videos by extending Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs) with a skeleton to apply to time-varying and articulated motion [S2, unofficial]. The method addresses the ill-posed inverse problem of mapping 3D world coordinates to a canonical space for articulated bodies by overparameterizing with one embedding per bone [S2, unofficial].
 
